WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.680
- Well, Tyler and I were
just talking about our kids

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:02.980
and you've got a daughter, right?

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:04.013
- I do, I have a--

00:00:04.013 --> 00:00:04.846
- [Kelly Clarkson] How old is she? Three?

00:00:04.846 --> 00:00:06.259
- A three and a half year old girl.

00:00:06.259 --> 00:00:07.092
- [Kelly Clarkson] Three and a half.

00:00:07.092 --> 00:00:07.925
- Yeah. Her name is Jackson.

00:00:07.925 --> 00:00:08.758
- [Kelly Clarkson] Oh.

00:00:08.758 --> 00:00:09.591
(audience swoons)

00:00:09.591 --> 00:00:10.990
- [Kelly Clarkson] oh my
God, look at that picture.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:11.823
- [Tyler Perry] Great age.

00:00:11.823 --> 00:00:14.070
- [Parker Young] Yeah we're
we're big Kelly Clarkson fans

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.270
in our household.

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:16.464
- Great taste (laughs)

00:00:16.464 --> 00:00:18.929
- I'm a little bit
embarrassed to say that uh,

00:00:18.929 --> 00:00:20.270
that I have spent too
many mornings dancing

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:21.190
to your music with her.

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:22.671
- [Kelly Clarkson] Oh my God.

00:00:22.671 --> 00:00:23.520
- This morning was, uh, Stronger.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.960
We were dancing, jamming out. She uh--

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.829
- I love that you do
that with your daughter.

00:00:27.829 --> 00:00:28.790
You're like, she's a daddy's girl.

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:30.593
- [Parker Young] Oh my goodness, yeah.

00:00:30.593 --> 00:00:31.426
She uh, she's like, can I come with you?

00:00:31.426 --> 00:00:32.259
I'm like, sorry, sweetheart.

00:00:32.259 --> 00:00:33.092
Not on this one,

00:00:33.092 --> 00:00:33.958
but

00:00:33.958 --> 00:00:34.791
- [Kelly Clarkson] Oh.

00:00:34.791 --> 00:00:36.163
- I told her I would
ask a question for her.

00:00:36.163 --> 00:00:36.996
- [Kelly Clarkson] Okay.

00:00:36.996 --> 00:00:37.829
- And her question is--

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:39.140
- Next time you should bring her.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:39.973
- I would love to.

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:41.119
- [Kelly Clarkson] Okay.

00:00:41.119 --> 00:00:42.397
- I would love to. Yeah uh,

00:00:42.397 --> 00:00:43.660
her question is what
is your favorite color?

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:45.160
- Oh, my favorite color is green.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:46.210
- [Parker Young] Green? Okay.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:47.603
Hers is gold sparkle.

00:00:48.514 --> 00:00:49.657
- [Kelly Clarkson] Gold sparkle.

00:00:49.657 --> 00:00:50.490
- Gold sparkle, yeah.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:51.323
- Oh my God that's so cute.

00:00:51.323 --> 00:00:52.156
There's a cute book she might like.

00:00:52.156 --> 00:00:52.989
Channing Tatum actually wrote it.

00:00:52.989 --> 00:00:54.050
It's called Sparkella.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:54.883
My kids love it.

00:00:54.883 --> 00:00:55.900
Anyway he was on here promoting it

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:56.733
and now I can't,

00:00:56.733 --> 00:00:58.197
I read it every night, thanks Channing.

00:00:58.197 --> 00:00:59.770
- He wrote it?

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:00.700
- Yeah, he wrote it.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:01.533
He has a little girl.

00:01:01.533 --> 00:01:02.930
but let's talk about your show.

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:04.780
So the show is powerful and timely.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:06.730
So um if people haven't seen it um,

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:07.860
kind of explain a little about.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:09.210
- Yeah, it's uh,

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.440
it's a show about a Marine um,

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.760
who's struggling to readjust
to civilian life in Ohio.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:16.310
He's living with his Afghan uh,

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:18.110
and one of his best friends
is the Afghan interpreter

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:18.990
that served with his unit.

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:21.090
That guy comes to the
states to start a new life.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:23.790
And the two of us are sort
of fumbling through this uh,

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:25.400
this next chapter in our lives.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:26.233
- Yeah.

00:01:26.233 --> 00:01:27.170
- I feel very grateful

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:28.450
that I have all these relationships with,

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:29.370
with um,

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:30.550
with a bunch of veterans and,

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:32.110
and active duty guys.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:34.610
I feel like it wouldn't
be my story to tell if I,

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.716
if I didn't have a lot of this experience.

00:01:36.716 --> 00:01:37.549
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yeah.

00:01:37.549 --> 00:01:38.382
- [Tyler Perry] You know
what's amazing about it?

00:01:38.382 --> 00:01:39.215
Chuck Lorre did this if I,

00:01:39.215 --> 00:01:40.190
if I'm not, if I'm not mistaken

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:42.890
he did this before everything
happened in Afghanistan.

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:43.928
- [Parker Young] Yeah.

00:01:43.928 --> 00:01:44.761
- [Kelly Clarkson] I know
that's what I was gonna ask you.

00:01:44.761 --> 00:01:45.594
So what happened,

00:01:45.594 --> 00:01:46.427
like when all that happened

00:01:46.427 --> 00:01:47.940
I know a lot of people are
trying to get loved ones out.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:48.773
- Yeah, it was,

00:01:48.773 --> 00:01:49.606
it was um,

00:01:49.606 --> 00:01:50.970
I mean first of all it was such an honor

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.410
to be in a position to try

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:55.070
and affect some semblance
of positive change

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:57.170
amidst that chaos and,
and, and destruction.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:59.760
But it was a really sad time as,

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.010
as you can imagine we
have a lot of Afghans

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:04.080
and Afghan Americans on set

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:07.185
both in front of the camera
and behind the camera.

00:02:07.185 --> 00:02:08.018
And they were devastated.

00:02:08.018 --> 00:02:08.851
I mean everyone was in tears.

00:02:08.851 --> 00:02:11.270
They're watching this
country that they love

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:13.900
disintegrate and be
taken over by the Taliban

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.300
and um.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.840
- And fearful for like family members.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:17.673
- So fearful.

00:02:17.673 --> 00:02:19.670
Yeah, so even though we were
in the middle of production,

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:22.660
priority number one became
trying to help our coworkers

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:24.580
get their loved ones outta the country

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:25.540
before it was too late.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:28.560
So, um, you know, me
and my coworker Adhir,

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:29.660
our military advisor,

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:31.490
and one of our Afghan writers flew to D.C.

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:33.620
to try to ask the president
to, to do everything

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.070
that he could to help these men and women

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:37.961
that have served our country
alongside our troops.

00:02:37.961 --> 00:02:38.794
- Mhm.

00:02:38.794 --> 00:02:40.490
- And um, our, our,

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:41.440
our military advisor,

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:42.470
guy named Chase Millsap,

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:44.130
he was on the phone day and night

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:46.730
with marines on the ground in Afghanistan

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:49.869
trying to get loved
ones out of the country.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:51.510
It was, it was chaos.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:52.770
- [Kelly Clarkson] That's a truly heroic.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:53.900
- [Parker Young] It was, it was heroic.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.640
And, and we were ultimately successful

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:57.250
and got a handful of people out.

00:02:57.250 --> 00:02:58.083
- That's great.

00:02:58.083 --> 00:02:58.916
- It was really cool.

00:02:58.916 --> 00:02:59.749
And then like uh.

00:02:59.749 --> 00:03:00.660
- Like if you do nothing
else in your life,

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:01.925
that is,

00:03:01.925 --> 00:03:02.758
what an amazing footprint.

00:03:02.758 --> 00:03:03.591
- I felt so great.

00:03:03.591 --> 00:03:05.890
And, and we ended up using
that experience to inspire our,

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:07.370
our season two premier episode,

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.070
which was about my character

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:10.510
and the interpreter getting,

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:12.270
fighting to get his sister out of country.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.850
So talk about art imitating life.

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:16.900
I mean, the lines really
started to blur there.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:18.837
- And I also love it's kind of similar,

00:03:18.837 --> 00:03:19.670
like the Madea thing.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:20.503
You take it's,

00:03:20.503 --> 00:03:21.380
it's a humorous show, it's a comedy.

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:22.213
- [Parker Young] Yeah.

00:03:22.213 --> 00:03:23.046
- But there are real messages happening.

00:03:23.046 --> 00:03:24.210
- Congrats by the way, man.

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:26.718
That's, that's on,
Madea coming to Netflix.

00:03:26.718 --> 00:03:27.551
- Oh. Thank you. Thank you.

00:03:27.551 --> 00:03:28.770
- [Parker Young] Such a fan.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:30.063
(audience claps)

00:03:30.063 --> 00:03:31.011
Yeah. I, I think that--

00:03:31.011 --> 00:03:31.844
- But hold on,

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:32.677
you can't compare Madea

00:03:32.677 --> 00:03:33.870
and rescuing people from Afghanistan.

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:35.113
I mean, come on.

00:03:35.113 --> 00:03:35.946
(audience laughs)

00:03:35.946 --> 00:03:36.779
- No, no, no I was saying like the fact

00:03:36.779 --> 00:03:37.612
that you have comedy though

00:03:37.612 --> 00:03:40.265
and you actually have a
message like with it as well.

00:03:40.265 --> 00:03:41.974
- You take real, heavy situations

00:03:41.974 --> 00:03:44.390
and you try to find a
way to make it funny.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.730
And I think there's nobody

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:46.988
that does it better than Tyler Perry.

00:03:46.988 --> 00:03:47.821
(audience claps and cheers)

00:03:47.821 --> 00:03:48.654
- [Kelly Clarkson] So funny.

00:03:48.654 --> 00:03:49.487
Amen.

